<TrustPage
  title="Corrections Policy"
  description="How factual errors, unclear explanations, broken sources, and material updates are reviewed and corrected."
>
  <h2>What should be reported</h2>
  <p>
    Havemoon welcomes reports of factual errors, outdated regulatory details, incorrect
    calculations, broken source links, ambiguous wording, or examples that may be mistaken for
    universal advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Review process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      The reported statement is compared with the cited source, publication context, and any current
      primary authority.
    </li>
    <li>The scope and practical impact of the issue are assessed.</li>
    <li>
      Confirmed errors are corrected in the article, related tools, and linked resources where
      applicable.
    </li>
    <li>
      The page update date is changed when the correction materially affects meaning or buyer
      action.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Correction notes</h2>
  <p>
    Minor spelling, formatting, or broken-link repairs may be made without a public note. Material
    corrections—such as a wrong responsibility, formula, effective date, or compliance
    statement—will be summarized on the affected page or in a dated correction log.
  </p>

  <h2>Submitting a correction</h2>
  <p class="trust-note">
    A verified public contact address will be added before launch. In this local preview, no
    unverified email address or contact identity is published.
  </p>
  <p>
    When the contact channel is active, a useful report should include the page URL, quoted
    statement, reason it may be wrong, and an authoritative source where available. Supplier
    marketing material alone may not be sufficient to change a regulatory claim.
  </p>
</TrustPage>
